dmenu - dynamic menu
====================

Personal dmenu build for X. It remains stock dmenu in normal use, with a few local UI patches used by the dwm keymap and launchers.

Change-size history
-------------------

See `scripts/cloc_by_commit.md` for changes since the upstream fork and per-change
runtime/support cloc counts. After editing, run
`python3 scripts/update_cloc_by_commit.py` (requires Python 3.9+, git, cloc).
It reports the latest totals/deltas and includes pending changes separately.
Use `--check` to detect stale reports; regenerate again after committing.

Build and install
-----------------

    make clean
    rm -f config.h
    make
    sudo make install

`config.h` is generated from `config.def.h`; this repo tracks both, so keep them synchronized.

Mint / Void
-----------

No distro detection or dwm session is required. Build with a compiler/make,
Xlib, Xft, Xinerama, fontconfig and FreeType headers. Mint package names include
libx11-dev, libxft-dev, libxinerama-dev, libfontconfig-dev and libfreetype-dev;
Void uses libX11-devel, libXft-devel, libXinerama-devel, fontconfig-devel and
freetype-devel. This menu also works under other X window managers.

Runtime font configuration
--------------------------

`make install` also installs the independent `dmenu-font` shell wrapper.
It reads the exact `dmenu.font` key from `xrdb -query` each time, falling back to
monospace:size=11. An explicit -fn argument takes precedence. dmenu_run uses the
wrapper when available; raw dmenu still uses compiled defaults/CLI options.

Set `dmenu.font: DroidSansM Nerd Font Mono:size=11` in an X resource file and
merge it with xrdb -merge. No rebuild is needed for subsequent changes. The
optional configure-sl session loads ~/.Xresources followed by the machine-local
~/.config/X11/machine.resources. No dwm or session framework is required.

Local changes
-------------

- Default font size adjusted for the local desktop.
- `-c` centers the menu on the selected monitor.
- Multiple-selection outline colors can be set with `-ob` and `-of`.

Upstream fixes backported
-------------------------

From https://git.suckless.org/dmenu (2026-09-13), retaining local centering
and smart-case behavior:

- `5453bb6`: guard horizontal drawing when a long prompt and End leave curr NULL.
- `0785a28`: reject zero Xinerama screens and fall back to screen 0 when the
  pointer intersects no screen. The fallback runs before centered placement.
- `61e0072`: require positive input length before inspecting the key buffer.

These are source backports, not a merge of upstream Git ancestry.

Usage
-----

Examples:

    dmenu_run
    printf '%s\n' one two three | dmenu -c -l 10 -p Choose:

See `dmenu.1` for all options and key bindings.
